From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:14:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: edge coverage emitted into each translated block when
 on

AFL-style edge coverage for fuzzing (map[prev ^ cur]++, prev = cur >> 1),
in the generated code so it counts every block however it is entered,
chained jumps included (a callback from cpu_tb_exec would only see the
first block of a chain).

translator_loop calls panda_cov_gen() once per block, before the first
instruction, only while panda_cov_on(): with coverage off (the default,
and always without --enable-panda, where both are empty inlines) the
only cost is one load and branch per block *translated*; generated code
is unchanged. The emitter, the map and the API live in the PANDA
overlay (src/panda/src/panda_cov.c).

CPUState gains panda_cov_prev, AFL's prev_loc, per vCPU so MTTCG vCPUs
don't interleave their edges. Generated code reaches it from tcg_env as
can_do_io is reached (offsetof - sizeof(CPUState)).

Same scheme as rehosting/qemu_builder's fastsnap coverage (patch 0018 on
workspace/fastsnap), written independently; that one keeps prev in a
host global and ids from the virtual pc.
---
 accel/tcg/translator.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 include/hw/core/cpu.h  |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/translator.c b/accel/tcg/translator.c
index d00bd8f21b9dede2204e4067c0f3d180111320f1..376f0bbeb811764ee6704efe2513edf592d8c47d 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/translator.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translator.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include "disas/disas.h"
 #include "tb-internal.h"
 #include "hooks-internal.h"
+#include "panda/hooks.h"
 
 static void set_can_do_io(DisasContextBase *db, bool val)
 {
@@ -154,6 +155,17 @@ void translator_loop(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *tb, int *max_insns,
     ops->tb_start(db, cpu);
     tcg_debug_assert(db->is_jmp == DISAS_NEXT);  /* no early exit */
 
+    /*
+     * Edge coverage, once per block ahead of its first instruction, so it
+     * counts however the block is entered (a chained jump too). Nothing is
+     * emitted unless coverage is on.
+     */
+#ifndef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
+    if (unlikely(panda_cov_on())) {
+        panda_cov_gen(db->tb, db->pc_first);
+    }
+#endif
+
     plugin_enabled = plugin_gen_tb_start(cpu, db);
     db->plugin_enabled = plugin_enabled;
 
diff --git a/include/hw/core/cpu.h b/include/hw/core/cpu.h
index 8033d4470b435a9a0a195b4ed6e10975752a4d12..15acca870bc5e40a2bed4e940c45595c2f2740a0 100644
--- a/include/hw/core/cpu.h
+++ b/include/hw/core/cpu.h
@@ -565,6 +565,8 @@ struct CPUState {
     int32_t exception_index;
     /* host return address into the block while a TCG hook runs, or 0 */
     uintptr_t tcg_hook_ra;
+    /* PANDA edge coverage: the previous block's id >> 1 (AFL's prev_loc), read by TCG code */
+    uint32_t panda_cov_prev;
     /*
      * A user-access window a plugin memory access opened and left open
      * across the guest fault it raised (plugins/api-system.c): the access
